Daily Mirror camera firmware: third-party notices

The license of the Daily Mirror project's own code is declared at the
repository root, not here. This file records what in this directory came from
somewhere else and under what terms.

1. components/esp_cam_sensor_imx/  (Apache-2.0)
   Vendored and trimmed from mushBrainDave/esp32-p4-imx-camera
   (https://github.com/mushBrainDave/esp32-p4-imx-camera), directory
   components/esp_cam_sensor_imx. The upstream LICENSE is kept in that
   directory. Changes: upstream's IMX219, IMX708 and DW9807 drivers removed;
   an IMX519 sensor driver (sensors/imx519/) and an AK7375 focus-motor driver
   (motors/ak7375/) added, written by following the structure of upstream's
   IMX708 and DW9807 drivers.

2. components/mirror_board/src/board_p4_imx519.c  (Apache-2.0)
   Portions of the capture-task and hardware-JPEG code are adapted from the
   same project's imx708_wifi_snapshot example.

3. components/esp_cam_sensor_imx/sensors/imx519/private_include/imx519_settings.h
   (GPL-2.0-only)
   IMX519 register initialisation tables taken verbatim from the Raspberry Pi
   Linux kernel driver drivers/media/i2c/imx519.c (Arducam Technology /
   Raspberry Pi Ltd). The file carries its own SPDX header and must not be
   relicensed. An ESP32-P4 firmware image that includes it should be treated
   as carrying GPL-2.0 source-availability obligations until this is resolved
   (see ../../docs/firmware-roadmap.md, "Open questions").

4. components/mirror_board/src/ov5640_af_cfg.h  (provenance unclear)
   OV5640 autofocus microcode and command-register definitions, copied from
   0015/ESP32-OV5640-AF (https://github.com/0015/ESP32-OV5640-AF). That
   repository's LICENSE is MIT and the file header says "released into the
   public domain", but the microcode itself is OmniVision's and its
   redistribution terms have not been established. Used on the ESP32-S3 board
   only. Resolve before distributing S3 firmware images.

5. Fetched at build time by the IDF component manager, not stored here:
   esp_cam_sensor, esp32-camera, esp_hosted, esp_wifi_remote, led_strip, mdns
   and their dependencies (Apache-2.0); esp_video and esp_ipa ("Espressif MIT
   License"). esp_ipa and esp_h264 link prebuilt static libraries.
